(32051, 1, '2026-01-16 11:49:37', '2026-01-16 11:49:37', '[vc_row css=\".vc_custom_1768564164950{border-bottom-width: 1px !important;border-bottom-style: solid !important;border-color: #2B204A !important;}\"][vc_column][vc_custom_heading text=\"THE ORIGIN OF THE GISÈLE DELORME PARIS BRAND - THE GISÈLE DELORME PARIS\" font_container=\"tag:h2|font_size:22px|text_align:left|color:%232B204A\" use_theme_fonts=\"yes\" css=\".vc_custom_1768563983393{margin-bottom: 40px !important;}\"][vc_row_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"1/3\"][vc_single_image image=\"32047\" img_size=\"full\" css=\"\"][/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=\"2/3\"][vc_column_text css=\"\"]From the very start of the Gisèle Delorme Paris brand in 1977, Madame Delorme was driven by the responsibility for results imposed on a professional brand and on the beautician using her method of treatment.\nThe concept she created need to provide remarkable results for every client, for every skin condition and in every situation.\nAnd right from the start, she incorporated the power of serums, a product category little known at the time of the brand’s creation. A visionary, Madame Delorme understood the benefits of these products for in-depth treatment. Her serums were all complex, and some incorporated phytotherapy.\nSince then, the Gisèle Delorme brand has become worldwide synonymous for beauty through skin health for a community of discerning women and men.\n\nThanks to its complete range of serums, it embodies made-to-measure skin care.[/vc_column_text][/vc_column_inner][/vc_row_inner][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'Who we are', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '32042-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-01-16 11:49:37', '2026-01-16 11:49:37', '', 32042, 'http://gisele.acutetest.com/?p=32051', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(287, 1, '2026-01-16 06:39:51', '2026-01-16 06:39:51', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Welcome to WordPress. This is your first post. Edit or delete it, then start writing!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Hello world!', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '1-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-01-16 06:39:51', '2026-01-16 06:39:51', '', 1, 'http://gisele.acutetest.com/?p=287', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(288, 1, '2026-01-16 06:39:51', '2026-01-16 06:39:51', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This is an example page. It\'s different from a blog post because it will stay in one place and will show up in your site navigation (in most themes). Most people start with an About page that introduces them to potential site visitors. It might say something like this:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\">\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Hi there! I\'m a bike messenger by day, aspiring actor by night, and this is my website. I live in Los Angeles, have a great dog named Jack, and I like pi&#241;a coladas. (And gettin\' caught in the rain.)</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>...or something like this:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\">\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The XYZ Doohickey Company was founded in 1971, and has been providing quality doohickeys to the public ever since. Located in Gotham City, XYZ employs over 2,000 people and does all kinds of awesome things for the Gotham community.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>As a new WordPress user, you should go to <a href=\"http://gisele.acutetest.com/wp-admin/\">your dashboard</a> to delete this page and create new pages for your content. Have fun!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Sample Page', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '2-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-01-16 06:39:51', '2026-01-16 06:39:51', '', 2, 'http://gisele.acutetest.com/?p=288', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
